meta {
  name: Read an offered document (reviewer)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/promotions/{{promoteDocId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  The document's actual text, so a reviewer can decide on what it says rather than on its
  title.

  This is the one deliberate exception to knowledge scopes: it returns a document that is
  still private to its author. It is sound because they explicitly offered it, and it is kept
  narrow — scoped to documents in `requested` state and to this endpoint alone. Retrieval is
  untouched, so an offered note is still unanswerable to anyone but its author.

  404 for any document that is not currently awaiting review — exactly as if it did not exist.
}
